AB  - The proceedings contain 13 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Enterprise and Organizational Modeling and Simulation. The topics include: SHACL shapes generation from textual documents; preface; designing an ontology for semantic integration of various conceptual models; Detection of declarative process constraints in LTL formulas; measures of quality in business process modeling; performance impact to the applying design patternization techniques to object-relational databases; Business process models (BPMN and DEMO Notation) - usability study; conceptual normalisation in software engineering; object-oriented class normalisation from a conceptual modelling perspective; evolvable and machine-actionable modular reports for service-oriented architecture; challenges in enterprise and information systems modeling in the contexts of socio cyber physical systems.
