AD  - Cheriton School of Computer Science, University of Waterloo, Waterloo, Canada
AB  - Earlier work has proposed a notion of referring expressions and types in first order knowledge bases as a way of more effectively answering conjunctive queries in ontology based data access (OBDA). We consider how PTIME description logics can be combined with referring expressions to provide a more effective virtual front-end to nested relational data sources via OBDA. In particular, we consider replacing the standard notion of an assertion box, or ABox, with a more general notion of a concept box, or CBox, and show how this can serve as a front-end to such data sources. © Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2019.
