AD  - Amity University, Amity Institute of Information Technology, Noida, Uttar Pradesh, India
AD  - University of Manouba, ISAMM - Riadi Lab.ISAMM, Tunis, Tunisia
AB  - Integrating Dengue patients' data in semantic web from 'deep web' facilitates interoperability amongst healthcare systems. Mapping dengue patients' data that exist in relational databases with the existing machine-readable and interoperable Dengue knowledge-base is crucial towards providing interoperability through linked data network amongst Electronic Health Record(EHR) systems. An RDB to RDF mapping language(R2RML) based approach that maps dengue patients' information maintained in legacy system(Relational database) to an existing dengue patients' ontology is proposed in this paper. Mapping file is generated using R2RML for the database which is subsequently customized and mapped with the existing ontology. Finally RDF model is generated using R2RML processor based on the customized ontology and Simple Protocol and RDF Query Language (SPARQL) query is also executed that demonstrates ontology mapped patients triples. © 2020 IEEE.
