AB  - The proceedings contain 44 papers. The topics discussed include: taming complex role inclusions for DL-Lite; temporal description logics over finite traces; towards privacy-preserving ontology publishing; efficient duplicate elimination in SPARQL to SQL translation; the Bayesian description logic BALC; a tool for building topic-specific ontologies using a knowledge graph; complete approximations of horn DL ontologies; computing minimal projection modules for conjunctive queries; computing best ontology excerpts via weighted partial Max-SAT solving; exact learning of EL ontologies; handling nominals and inverse roles using algebraic reasoning; from conjunctive queries to SPARQL queries in ontology-mediated querying; a dynamic extension of ALCO for repairing via preferred updates; concepts as modal operators in description logics; ontology partitioning using e-connections revisited; preferential default reasoning on the semantic web; on the data complexity of ontology-mediated queries with MTL operators over timed words; generating ontologies from templates: a rule-based approach for capturing regularity; cutting diamonds: temporal DLS with probabilistic distributions over data; ABox abduction solver exploiting multiple dl reasoners; comparing query answering in OBDA tools over W3C-compliant specifications; verifying contract-based specifications of product lines using description logic; happy ever after: temporally attributed description logics; provenance in ontology-based data access; SIVA: an educational tool for the tableau reasoning algorithm; applying a model of text comprehension to automated verbalizations of EL derivations; and standard and non-standard inferences in the description logic FL0 using tree automata.
