AB  - The proceedings contain 27 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Model and Data Engineering. The topics include: Transformation of anti-rigid sortal types into relational databases; automatic generation of ecore models for testing ATL transformations; towards a methodological tool support for modeling security-oriented processes; a heuristic-based data format selector for intermediate results; a meta-advisor repository for database physical design; linked service selection using the skyline algorithm; toward multi criteria optimization of business processes design; semantic-enabled and hypermedia-driven linked service discovery; maintenance of profile matchings in knowledge bases; distributed reasoning for mapped ontologies using rewriting logic; towards a formal validation of ETL patterns behaviour; building OLAP cubes from columnar NOSQL data warehouses; on representing interval measures by means of functions; automated data pre-processing via meta-learning; incremental approach for detecting arbitrary and embedded cluster structures; annotation of engineering models by references to domain ontologies; unifying warehoused data with linked open data; correct-by-construction evolution of realisable conversation protocols; white-box modernization of legacy applications; exploring quality-aware architectural transformations at run-time; a credibility and classification-based approach for opinion analysis in social networks; engineering applications over social and open data with domain-specific languages and word similarity based on domain graph.
