AB  - The proceedings contain 32 papers. The topics discussed include: ontology of monotheism road map to reach the OntoM; applying meta-modelling to an accounting application; a measurement ontology for beliefs, desires, intentions and feelings within knowledge-intensive processes; ontologies in category theory: a search for meaningful morphisms; ontological representation of relational databases; annotating diverse scientific data with HAScO; building an ontology network to support environmental quality research: first steps; ontology integration approaches: a systematic mapping; using an ontology network for data integration: a case in the public security domain; toward an ontological analysis of archetypal entities in the marketing domain: personas and related concepts; I2oTology - tracking-oriented ontology; mapping refinement based on ontology evolution: a context-matching approach; CM-OPL: an ontology pattern language for the configuration management task; and towards a conceptual model for Brazilian popular music representation.
