AB  - The proceedings contain 46 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Conceptual Modeling. The topics include: The common ontology of value and risk; Endurant types in ontology-driven conceptual modeling: Towards ontoUML 2.0; reification and truthmaking patterns; conceptual modeling of legal relations; inferring deterministic regular expression with counting; towards quality analysis for document oriented bases; a holistic approach for soundness verification of decision-aware process models; conceptual modeling of processes and data: Connecting different perspectives; interactive data-driven process model construction; recent trends of big data platforms and applications; efficient multi-range query processing on trajectories; a volunteer design methodology of data warehouses; using a conceptual model to transform road networks from openstreetmap to a graph database; Modeling conceptual characteristics of virtual machines for CPU utilization prediction; towards the design of a scalable business process management system architecture in the cloud; towards an ontology of software defects, errors and failures; TemporalEMF: A temporal metamodeling framework; A semantic framework for designing temporal SQL databases; Nested schema mappings for integrating JSON; multi-level conceptual modeling: from a formal theory to a well-founded language; conceptual modeling on tencent’s distributed database systems; Increasing the semantic transparency of the KAOS goal model concrete syntax; using contextual goal models for constructing situational methods; multi-perspective comparison of business process variants based on event logs; managing polyglot systems metadata with hypergraphs; Renormalization of NoSQL database schemas; Modeling strategies for storing data in distributed heterogeneous NoSQL databases; how the conceptual modelling improves the security on document databases; ontological deep data cleaning.
