AD  - Institute of Production Engineering and Laser Technology - TU Wien, Getreidemarkt 9, Vienna, 1060, Austria
AD  - Institute of Information Systems Engineering - TU Wien, Favoritenstrasse 9-11, Vienna, 1040, Austria
AB  - Time-series based simulations of industrial processes are instrumental to optimizing a variety of industrial settings. In this paper, we describe a use case, developed together with Infineon Technologies Austria AG. Monitoring data stored in relational databases was used to build process models of industrial chillers. Optimization algorithms were then applied to find optimal strategies for operating the chillers. Even though the results from this approach were convincing, the access to the necessary data was a labor-intensive and error-prone task. Therefore, in this paper, we investigate how Semantic Web technologies can help to improve data access for time-series data and under which circumstances they would be helpful for the domain experts performing the simulation. © 2018 CEUR-WS. All Rights Reserved.
