AB  - The proceedings contain 99 papers. The topics discussed include: an open question answering framework; SPARQLT and its user-friendly interface for managing and querying the history of RDF knowledge bases; OTTO ontology translation system; automatic SPARQL benchmark generation using FEASIBLE; ANNA: answering WhyNot questions for SPARQL; BootOX: bootstrapping OWL 2 ontologies and R2RML mappings from relational databases; intermodal public transit routing using linked connections; a webtool for analyzing land-use planning documents; Datavore: a vocabulary recommender tool assisting linked data modeling; rSim: simplifying an RDF graph at the visualization tier for non-expert users; ExConQuer framework softening RDF data to enhance linked data reuse; BASIL: a cloud platform for sharing and reusing SPARQL queries as web APIs; semantically-enabled personal medical information recommender; and demonstrating the power of streaming and sorting for non-distributed RDF processing: RDFpro.
