AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers. The special focus in this conference is on E-business, E-services, and E-society. The topics include: Order effects in observations of stated and revealed privacy preferences; a user privacy protection technique for executing SQL over encrypted data in database outsourcing service; assessing emotions related to privacy and trust in personalized services; trust and privacy in the shift from e-commerce to m-commerce; a cloud provider description schema for meeting legal requirements in cloud federation scenarios; identifying the major security and privacy concerns; a methodology for the development and verification of access control systems in cloud computing; simple mail delivery protocol; analysis of social network dynamics with models from the theory of complex adaptive systems; evaluation of spectrum rights for radio broadcasting operators; SWOT analysis of a Portuguese electronic health record; discovering authentication credentials in volatile memory of android mobile devices; conceptualizing perceived benefits and investigating its role in adoption of tablet computers among newspaper subscribers; designing to promote a new social affordance for energy consumption; coupons as monetary incentives in participatory sensing; foundational ontologies for semantic integration in eai; developing innovative services; creating knowledge within a c-business context; designing and developing a business continuity plan based on collective intelligence; rewarding in-game banner ad clicks with tangible incentives; designing visual exemplars of 3D online store layout types; a multicriteria methodology for the selection and prioritisation of public services and e-government benchmarking in European union.
