AD  - Database Center for Life Science, Univ. of Tokyo, Kashiwa-no-ha Campus Station Satellite 6F, 178-4-4 Wakashiba, Kashiwa-shi, Chiba, Japan
AB  - D2RQ Mapper (http://d2rq.dbcls.jp/) is a web application to edit a mapping file of D2RQ, a middleware to bridge Relational Database (RDB) and Resource Description Framework (RDF). A D2RQ mapping file defines how to map data stored in an RDB to RDF in the turtle format, and to write it by a text editor is cumbersome. D2RQ Mapper assists you to edit it by contextualizing input forms in the mapping language. In addition, D2RQ Mapper supports the R2RML format to output a mapping definition. We provide a Docker image of D2RQ Mapper, and so you can easily use it within your intranet. © Copyright 2015 for the individual papers by the papers' authors.
