AD  - KISTI, 245 Daehak-ro, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon, South Korea
AD  - Sangmyung Univ, 20Hongjimun2-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, South Korea
AB  - The R2RML standard provides an ability to view existing relational data in the RDF data model. However, it is inadequate to express mappings in case that the underlying database schema changes dynamically and frequently. To deal with this issue, we present an extension of the R2RML, where variables are allowed to be defined and values of the variables are retrieved from an SQL. And we introduce an efficient translation technique and its implementation from SPARQL into SQL with the extended R2RML, which is able to manage database schema changes. The implementation is applied to a tag metadata catalog service, called a Tagfiler. © Research India Publications.
