AB  - The proceedings contain 27 papers. The topics discussed include: the complexity of mining maximal frequent subgraphs; deciding monotone duality and identifying frequent itemsets in quadratic logspace; spanners: a formal framework for information extraction; verification of database-driven systems via amalgamation; sketching via hashing: from heavy hitters to compressive sensing to sparse Fourier transform; collaborative data-driven workflows: think global, act local; I/O-efficient planar range skyline and attrition priority queues; on the expressive power of update primitives; verification of relational data-centric dynamic systems with external services; ontology-based data access: a study through disjunctive datalog, CSP, and MMSNP; well-founded semantics for extended datalog and ontological reasoning; semantic acyclicity on graph databases; and a dichotomy in the intensional expressive power of nested relational calculi augmented with aggregate functions and a powerset operator.
