AB  - The proceedings contain 48 papers. The topics discussed include: querying and reasoning about massive social networks; on probabilistic record linkage: new methods compared to the Fellegi-Sunter approach; answering queries in a relaxed way; a fast and accurate algorithm for hierarchical clustering on Euclidean distances; clustering of process schemas by graph mining techniques; supporting roll-up and drill-down operations over OLAP data cubes with continuous dimensions via density-based hierarchical clustering; a decomposition technique for the inverse frequent itemset mining problem; computing multi-dimensional OLAP data cubes over probabilistic relational data: a decomposition approach; on provenance of data fusion queries; on equality-generating dependencies in ontology querying; keyword-based search in data integration systems; and querying compressed knowledge bases in pervasive computing.
