AB  - The proceedings contain 22 papers. The topics discussed include: simplified access control policies for XML databases; on separability of ontological constraints; ontology contraction: beyond the propositional paradise; semantics of constraints in RDFS; on low treewidth approximations of conjunctive queries; temporal SOLAP: query language, implementation, and a use case; on the logic of SQL nulls; union and intersection of schema mappings; multi-granular schemas for data integration; on the translatability of view updates; chasing polarized order dependencies; relative expressiveness of nested regular expressions; multidimensional contexts for data quality assessment; towards analytical data management for numerical simulations; automatic filling of web forms; semantic loss in query reformulation in dynamic distributed environments; and enriching query routing processes in PDMS with semantic information and information quality.
