AB  - The proceedings contain 58 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Query Transformation and Data Mining. The topics include: Infrastructure for the information space; a reason-able web ontology language; plenty of challenges by 2010; an approach to integrating query refinement in SQL; querying with intrinsic preferences; rewriting unions of general conjunctive queries using views; from patterns to actions; cut-and-pick transactions for proxy log mining; composition of mining contexts for efficient extraction of association rules; designing functional dependencies for XML; on efficient matching of streaming XML documents and queries; efficient complex query support for multiversion XML documents; approximate processing of multiway spatial joins in very large databases; indexing values in continuous field databases; efficient and adaptive processing of multiple continuous queries; the geometry of uncertainty in moving objects databases; efficient indexing of spatiotemporal objects; dynamic queries over mobile objects; semantic analysis of business process executions; an introduction to the e-XML data integration suite; spatio-temporal information systems in a statistical context; a systematic approach to selecting maintenance policies in a data warehouse environment; efficient OLAP Query Processing in Distributed Data Warehouses; incremental maintenance of schema-restructuring views; coupling of FDBS and WfMS for integrating database and application systems; optimizing scientific databases for client side data processing; supporting efficient parametric search of E-commerce data; divide-and-conquer algorithm for computing set containment joins; universal quantification in relational databases; efficient algorithms for mining inclusion dependencies and tree pattern relaxation.
